From: Fco Javier Felix <ffelix@inode64.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:13:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] util: install the ras-mc-ctl helpers outside
 site-packages

py.install_sources() puts the helper modules at the top level of
site-packages:

  /usr/lib/python3.14/site-packages/__init__.py
  /usr/lib/python3.14/site-packages/display_table.py
  /usr/lib/python3.14/site-packages/mem_layout.py
  /usr/lib/python3.14/site-packages/ras_config.py
  ...

They are not a Python package: ras-mc-ctl adds PYTHON_DIR to sys.path
and imports them by name. At that level, though, every Python program
sees them, generic names such as display_table or mem_layout can clash
with other modules, and the __init__.py does not belong to any
package. The directory is also the one of the interpreter Meson found
at build time, which ras-mc-ctl then hard-codes.

Install them in <datadir>/rasdaemon, where private modules usually go.
ras-mc-ctl already adds PYTHON_DIR to sys.path, so nothing else
changes, and the Debian note about dist-packages no longer applies.
install_data() does not byte-compile, so the spec does it with
%py_byte_compile.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01N8fTR5eZWWPFd2fewTXKDt
Signed-off-by: Fco Javier Felix <ffelix@inode64.com>
---
 meson.build            | 4 +++-
 misc/rasdaemon.spec.in | 4 ++--
 util/meson.build       | 4 ++--
 util/ras-mc-ctl.py     | 6 ++----
 4 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index ffee622..ec88f10 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -69,7 +69,9 @@ arch_x86 = arch == 'all' or arch == 'x86'
 arch_arm = arch == 'all' or arch == 'arm'
 arch_riscv = arch == 'all' or arch == 'riscv'
 
-pydir = py.get_install_dir(pure: true)
+# ras-mc-ctl adds this directory to sys.path: its helpers are not a public
+# Python package, so they stay out of site-packages.
+pydir = prefix / datadir / meson.project_name()
 
 #
 # Global dependencies and install directory paths
diff --git a/misc/rasdaemon.spec.in b/misc/rasdaemon.spec.in
index 6cfc451..ffa55e7 100644
--- a/misc/rasdaemon.spec.in
+++ b/misc/rasdaemon.spec.in
@@ -67,13 +67,13 @@ an utility for reporting current error counts from the EDAC sysfs files.
 
 %install
 %meson_install
+%py_byte_compile %{python3} %{buildroot}%{_datadir}/%{name}
 
 %files
 %doc AUTHORS ChangeLog COPYING README.rst SECURITY.rst TODO
 %{_sbindir}/%{name}
 %{_sbindir}/ras-mc-ctl
-%{python3_sitelib}/*.py
-%{python3_sitelib}/__pycache__/*
+%{_datadir}/%{name}/
 %{_mandir}/*/*
 %{_unitdir}/*.service
 %{_sysconfdir}/ras/*/*
diff --git a/util/meson.build b/util/meson.build
index ab56d37..a9ff47b 100644
--- a/util/meson.build
+++ b/util/meson.build
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 #
 # Copyright (C) 2026 Mauro Carvalho Chehab <mchehab+huawei@kernel.org>
 
-py.install_sources([
+install_data([
     '__init__.py',
     'display_table.py',
     'mem_layout.py',
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@ py.install_sources([
     'ras_filter.py',
     'ras_dimm.py',
     'ras_env.py',
-])
+], install_dir: pydir)
 
 ras_mc_ctl_conf = configuration_data()
 ras_mc_ctl_conf.set('PYTHON_DIR', pydir)
diff --git a/util/ras-mc-ctl.py b/util/ras-mc-ctl.py
index 417cb5a..a5d2ff2 100755
--- a/util/ras-mc-ctl.py
+++ b/util/ras-mc-ctl.py
@@ -13,10 +13,8 @@ import logging
 import os
 import sys
 
-# Debian's Python does not include /usr/local/lib/python3/dist-packages in
-# sys.path, although that is where its sysconfig scheme (and therefore Meson)
-# installs prefix-independent modules.  Add the configured installation path
-# explicitly so the default /usr/local prefix and custom prefixes both work.
+# The helper modules are installed in a private directory, outside sys.path.
+# RAS_PYTHON_DIR overrides it, for instance to run from the build tree.
 python_dir = os.environ.get('RAS_PYTHON_DIR', '@PYTHON_DIR@')
 if python_dir not in sys.path:
     sys.path.insert(0, python_dir)
